  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;angles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>Also, by angle sum property&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>By, using sine rule, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;and hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is a right triangle, with hypotenuse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Again, by Sine rule, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6a9ebb1e-56c5-4aab-9a40-e1000bb86a66-image4.png\" /></p><p>Now, the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mi>base</mi></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mi>height</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
